  <owl:Class rdf:about="#tsk_4a57abb9498ef">
    <dc:identifier>tsk_4a57abb9498ef</dc:identifier>
    <skos:prefLabel>boston naming test</skos:prefLabel>
    <rdfs:label>boston naming test</rdfs:label>
    <skos:definition>assesses the ability to name pictures of objects through spontaneous responses and need for various types of cueing, inferences can be drawn regarding language facility and possible localization of cerebral damage.</skos:definition>
    <dc:Contributor>usr_51bc76ae9636c</dc:Contributor>
    <dc:Title>boston naming test</dc:Title>
    <dc:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1512660583744</dc:date>
    <skos:altLabel>BNT</skos:altLabel>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="#trm_553e73e29cf7d">
    <dc:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1512660597803</dc:date>
    <skos:definition>This task presents blocks of fixation and words, with the words varying in the degree to which they are predictable (given the context of the previous words). On each trial, a fixation cross is presented followed by a visual prompt (asterisk) and a sequence of five centrally presented words (in lower case). The experimental variable is the predictability of the terminal, target word, represented in four conditions (Congruent == highly predictable,Incongruent == target word is highly predictable, but the prediction was violated by presenting a terminal word that was inappropriate given the context, Scrambled == initial four words did not establish a context for a grammatical sentence and the target word was not predictable, and Letter String == meaningless letter strings of identical consonants as a control). After presentation of the target word, the participant is asked if the sentence is meaningful. The above description was derived from (and full details are available) here: http://www.jneurosci.org/content/34/8/2871.full</skos:definition>
    <dc:identifier>trm_553e73e29cf7d</dc:identifier>
    <dc:Title>contextual semantic priming task</dc:Title>
    <rdfs:label>contextual semantic priming task</rdfs:label>
    <dc:Contributor>usr_51bc76ae9636c</dc:Contributor>
    <skos:prefLabel>contextual semantic priming task</skos:prefLabel>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="#trm_4da88c205b16b">
    <dc:Contributor>usr_4f177506dde77</dc:Contributor>
    <rdfs:label>haptic illusion task</rdfs:label>
    <dc:Title>haptic illusion task</dc:Title>
    <dc:identifier>trm_4da88c205b16b</dc:identifier>
    <skos:definition>cognitive and physiological measures are taken while participant experiences a tactile illusion</skos:definition>
    <skos:prefLabel>haptic illusion task</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1512660588219</dc:date>
    <skos:altLabel>tactile illusion</skos:altLabel>
  </owl:Class>
