  <owl:Class rdf:about="#trm_523ca7e778c50">
    <skos:definition>focusing negative energy on the self, often through holding back emotion, often leading to less than ideal emotional states (worry, anxiety, negativity and depression).  These states are frequently present in autistic children.</skos:definition>
    <skos:prefLabel>internalizing</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:altLabel>worry, anxiety, negativity, depression</skos:altLabel>
    <dc:Contributor>usr_51bc76ae9636c</dc:Contributor>
    <dc:Title>internalizing</dc:Title>
    <dc:Date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1512660641076</dc:Date>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="#trm_4aae62e4ad209">
    <dc:Date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1512660638510</dc:Date>
    <skos:altLabel>executive control, executive function</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:hasTopConcept rdf:resource="#ctp_C4"/>
    <skos:prefLabel>cognitive control</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:Contributor>usr_51bc76ae9636c</dc:Contributor>
    <skos:definition>The top-down modulation of cognitive processes based on higher-order representations such as goals or plans.</skos:definition>
    <dc:Title>cognitive control</dc:Title>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="#trm_521687032f822">
    <skos:definition>The Social Communication Questionnaire consists of 40 yes/no questions (answered by parents) to screen for autism spectrum disorders in children four years of age and older.  Specifically, the questions ask about social functioning and communication skills.  Two forms of the SCQ include the Lifetime and Current, which assesst behaviors for each of those periods. &#13;
&#13;
Theoretically derived subscales include 1) Reciprocal Social Interaction subscale, 2) Communication subscale, and 3) Restricted, Repetitive, and Stereotyped Patterns of Behavior subscale, although they have not been formally validated.&#13;
&#13;
Questions 20 through 40 (Lifetime) focus on behaviors occurring between the ages of 4 and 5.&#13;
Total scores can range from 0 to 39&#13;
The first question is a language screening item that is not included in the final score.&#13;
Total SCQ raw score of â¥ 15 is highly suggestive of ASD</skos:definition>
    <dc:identifier>trm_521687032f822</dc:identifier>
    <dc:Contributor>usr_51bc76ae9636c</dc:Contributor>
    <skos:prefLabel>Social Communication Questionnaire</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:Title>Social Communication Questionnaire</dc:Title>
    <rdfs:label>Social Communication Questionnaire</rdfs:label>
    <dc:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1512660594194</dc:date>
    <skos:altLabel>SCQ, Autism Screening Questionnaire, ASQ</skos:altLabel>
  </owl:Class>
