  <owl:Class rdf:about="#trm_56a2a98785453">
    <skos:prefLabel>Penn Visual Object Learning Test Delayed Memory</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:Title>Penn Visual Object Learning Test Delayed Memory</dc:Title>
    <dc:Contributor>usr_569fc42c3002f</dc:Contributor>
    <skos:definition>The delayed memory portion of the sVOLT tasj. &#13;
&#13;
In the first part of this test, participants were shown 10 three-dimensional Euclidean shapes that they were asked to identify for immediate recall (sVOLT . Now, during the delayed recall (sVOLTd , participants are shown a series, one at a time, of 20 three-dimensional Euclidean shapes - the 10 shapes they were asked to memorize during the SVOLT mixed with 10 novel shapes. The participantâs task is to decide whether he/she has seen the shape before by clicking with the mouse on one of four buttons: âDEFINITELY YESâ, âPROBABLY YESâ, &amp;#34;PROBABLY NO&amp;#34; and &amp;#34;DEFINITELY NO&amp;#34;. (NOTE: The original sVOLT had only two response choices: âYES I have seen the shapeâ and âNO I have not seen the shape.â . Participants have 20 seconds to select a response before the test moves on to the next trial. There are two forms of the sVOLTd: the sVOLTd-A and sVOLTd-B.&#13;
</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:label>Penn Visual Object Learning Test Delayed Memory</rdfs:label>
    <skos:altLabel>sVOLTd, Short VOLT delay, VOLTd, sVOLTd</skos:altLabel>
    <dc:identifier>trm_56a2a98785453</dc:identifier>
    <dc:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1512660599952</dc:date>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="#trm_551b0c0a742d2">
    <skos:prefLabel>lateral facilitation</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:Title>lateral facilitation</dc:Title>
    <dc:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1512660596383</dc:date>
    <dc:Contributor>usr_4e42a3196fbcd</dc:Contributor>
    <rdfs:label>lateral facilitation</rdfs:label>
    <skos:definition>None</skos:definition>
    <dc:identifier>trm_551b0c0a742d2</dc:identifier>
  </owl:Class>
