  <owl:Class rdf:about="#trm_515495b718cd6">
    <dc:Contributor>usr_595048b29ebdf</dc:Contributor>
    <dc:identifier>trm_515495b718cd6</dc:identifier>
    <skos:altLabel>Dot Pattern Expectancy,Dot Probe Expectancy</skos:altLabel>
    <dc:Title>AX-DPX</dc:Title>
    <skos:definition>An alternative version of the AX-CPT in which the letter stimuli are replaced with simple dot patterns derived from Braille language. Dot patterns are more easily parametrically manipulated, and require less time between stimuli presentations because they are not as easily stored in working memory as letters, thus increasing the proportion of errors.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:label>AX-DPX</rdfs:label>
    <skos:prefLabel>AX-DPX</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1512660593850</dc:date>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="#trm_553fcbbe974ba">
    <skos:prefLabel>stop signal walking task with stroop</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:Contributor>usr_51bc76ae9636c</dc:Contributor>
    <dc:Title>stop signal walking task with stroop</dc:Title>
    <dc:identifier>trm_553fcbbe974ba</dc:identifier>
    <dc:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1512660598207</dc:date>
    <rdfs:label>stop signal walking task with stroop</rdfs:label>
    <skos:definition>Participants walk around a virtual reality environment controlled by a foot pedal and must respond to STOP and WALK commands. In a low cognitive load condition, participants respond to these commands verbatim. In a high cognitive load condition, participants are presented with stroop stimuli, and congruent words == WALK, and incongruent words == STOP. Full details: http://journals.plos.org/plosone/article?id=10.1371/journal.pone.0052602</skos:definition>
  </owl:Class>
