  <owl:Class rdf:about="#trm_4d54b8361e93e">
    <dc:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1512660586780</dc:date>
    <dc:Contributor>usr_595048b29ebdf</dc:Contributor>
    <dc:Title>behavioral investment allocation strategy</dc:Title>
    <skos:altLabel>BIAS</skos:altLabel>
    <dc:identifier>trm_4d54b8361e93e</dc:identifier>
    <skos:definition>On each trial, participants choose between two stocks (gain/loss gambles, one stochastically dominating the other) and one bond (a sure gain of $1). They must learn through trial-and-error the characteristics of the stocks, which change over blocks of trials. Feedback on payoffs of the forgone options is presented on each trial. </skos:definition>
    <skos:prefLabel>behavioral investment allocation strategy</skos:prefLabel>
    <rdfs:label>behavioral investment allocation strategy</rdfs:label>
  </owl:Class>
