  <owl:Class rdf:about="#trm_50f383e76e03b">
    <dc:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1512660593114</dc:date>
    <dc:Contributor>usr_4de5345b3b6a8</dc:Contributor>
    <dc:identifier>trm_50f383e76e03b</dc:identifier>
    <dc:Title>NIH Toolbox Odor Identification Test</dc:Title>
    <rdfs:label>NIH Toolbox Odor Identification Test</rdfs:label>
    <skos:definition>This task assesses a personâs ability to identify various odors. Participants use scratch-andsniff cards and after scratching them one at a time, are asked to identify which of four pictures on the computer screen matches the odor they have just smelled. Participants ages 10-85 are administered nine odor cards, while those ages 3-9 are administered five odor cards. Child participants (ages 3-9 years) are first asked to identify the eight pictures used as answer choices to ensure they can complete the task. Having identified the pictures, they are asked if they have tasted or smelled the objects or foods depicted.</skos:definition>
    <skos:prefLabel>NIH Toolbox Odor Identification Test</skos:prefLabel>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="#trm_4fbd2c18e1dd9">
    <dc:Contributor>usr_4f177506dde77</dc:Contributor>
    <skos:definition>participants are shown pictures and asked to identify whether the object could be real or is unreal</skos:definition>
    <dc:identifier>trm_4fbd2c18e1dd9</dc:identifier>
