  <owl:Class rdf:about="#trm_4a3fd79d0b8d9">
    <skos:definition>a type of rehearsal proposed by Craik and Lockhart (1972) in their Levels of Processing model of memory. Elaborative rehearsal involves deep semantic processing of a to-be-remembered item resulting in the production of durable memories.</skos:definition>
