  <owl:Class rdf:about="#trm_4a3fd79d0a375">
    <skos:prefLabel>fluid intelligence</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:Date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1512660630420</dc:Date>
    <skos:hasTopConcept rdf:resource="#ctp_C3"/>
    <skos:altLabel>fluid reasoning</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:definition>a factor of general intelligence originally identified by Raymond Cattell; Cattell defined fluid intelligence as &amp;#34;â¦the ability to perceive relationships independent of previous specific practice or instruction concerning those relationships.&amp;#34; Fluid intelligence is the ability to think and reason abstractly and solve problems. This ability is considered independent of learning, experience, and education.</skos:definition>
    <dc:Title>fluid intelligence</dc:Title>
    <dc:Contributor>usr_595048b29ebdf</dc:Contributor>
