  <owl:Class rdf:about="#trm_4a3fd79d0a4a6">
    <dc:Date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1512660630894</dc:Date>
    <skos:prefLabel>hallucination</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:Contributor>usr_4cf5de07654c8</dc:Contributor>
    <dc:Title>hallucination</dc:Title>
    <skos:definition>in the broadest sense of the word, is a perception in the absence of a stimulus. In a stricter sense, hallucinations are defined as perceptions in a conscious and awake state in the absence of external stimuli which have qualities of real perception, in that they are vivid, substantial, and located in external objective space.&#13;
&#13;
</skos:definition>
  </owl:Class>
