  <owl:Class rdf:about="#trm_4a3fd79d0ac61">
    <dc:Date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1512660633567</dc:Date>
    <skos:prefLabel>phonological buffer</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:Title>phonological buffer</dc:Title>
    <skos:hasTopConcept rdf:resource="#ctp_C6"/>
    <dc:Contributor>usr_49a467bf4e0db</dc:Contributor>
    <skos:definition>a passive storage device that is part of the articulatory rehearsal loop; serves as a part of the mechanisms ordinarily needed for hearing.  In rehearsal, the buffer is loaded by means of subvocalization.</skos:definition>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="#tsk_4a57abb949d84">
    <skos:definition>Participants read or listen to sentences, then judge whether the sentence is plausible and makes sense semantically, or is implausible. Sentences may be structurally and gramatically correct, but the verb and noun are incompatible. Often, the structure or length of sentences varies to assess the role of working memory in any resulting deficit. </skos:definition>
    <skos:prefLabel>semantic anomaly judgement task</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:Title>semantic anomaly judgement task</dc:Title>
    <rdfs:label>semantic anomaly judgement task</rdfs:label>
    <dc:Contributor>usr_4de5345b3b6a8</dc:Contributor>
    <dc:identifier>tsk_4a57abb949d84</dc:identifier>
    <dc:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1512660585646</dc:date>
  </owl:Class>
