  <owl:Class rdf:about="#trm_586fd4fd8754a">
    <skos:definition>The subject views a flashing checkerboard with a horizontal elongated shape. As a simplified retinotopic mapping procedure, this provides a rough definition of the boundary between some visual areas, e.g. V2 and V3. This is often used in conjunction and contrasted with vertical checkerboards. </skos:definition>
    <skos:prefLabel>horizontal checkerboard</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:Title>horizontal checkerboard</dc:Title>
    <rdfs:label>horizontal checkerboard</rdfs:label>
