  <owl:Class rdf:about="#trm_4a3fd79d09a3d">
    <dc:Title>auditory coding</dc:Title>
    <dc:Date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1512660627153</dc:Date>
    <skos:definition>processing and encoding of sound, words, and all other auditory input for storage and later retrieval. According to Baddeley, processing of auditory information is aided by the concept of the phonological loop, which allows input within our echoic memory.</skos:definition>
