  <owl:Class rdf:about="#trm_56a2a665baeb1">
    <dc:Contributor>usr_595048b29ebdf</dc:Contributor>
    <skos:definition>A measure of delayed word memory. In the first part of this test, participants are shown 20 words that they were asked to identify for immediate recall (CPW . Now, during the delayed recall, participants are shown a series, one at a time, of 40 words: the 20 study stimuli they were asked to memorize and 20 novel stimuli, completely different from the 20 distracters showed on the CPW. The participantsâ task is to decide whether they have seen the word before by clicking one of four buttons, presented in a 4-point scale: âdefinitely yesâ, âprobably yesâ, âprobably noâ and âdefinitely no,â using the mouse. There is one alternate form of the CPWd: the CPWd-b.&#13;
</skos:definition>
    <skos:prefLabel>Adult's Penn Word Memory Test Delayed Memory</skos:prefLabel>
    <dc:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1512660599727</dc:date>
    <dc:Title>Adult's Penn Word Memory Test Delayed Memory</dc:Title>
    <dc:identifier>trm_56a2a665baeb1</dc:identifier>
    <rdfs:label>Adult's Penn Word Memory Test Delayed Memory</rdfs:label>
    <skos:altLabel>CPWd, CPWdelay</skos:altLabel>
  </owl:Class>
