  <owl:Class rdf:about="#trm_4a3fd79d0a006">
    <dc:Title>dative shift</dc:Title>
    <dc:Date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1512660629213</dc:Date>
    <skos:hasTopConcept rdf:resource="#ctp_C6"/>
    <dc:Contributor>usr_49a467bf4e0db</dc:Contributor>
    <skos:prefLabel>dative shift</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:definition>a grammatical process by which an oblique  argument of a verb, usually one functioning as a recipient or a benefactive (roles often expressed by datives), is placed in the same grammatical role as a patient, increasing the valency of the verb and forming a clause with two objects.</skos:definition>
  </owl:Class>
